        "original_id": "a2f8e555-8f49-5a60-901b-b640806a2e7b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Rani Jhansi Marine National Park, Middle Button Island National Park, Jhansi, North India, Jhansi district, Uttar Pradesh, South Andaman Island\n- People: Lakshmibai, the Rani of Jhansi\n- Places: North Button Island, South Button Island\n- Topics: commemoration, national parks\n\nFacts:\n- Lakshmibai, the Rani of Jhansi, was born on 19 November 1828 and died on 18 June 1858.\n- Lakshmibai, the Rani of Jhansi, was the queen of the princely state of Jhansi in North India, in the area now in Jhansi district, Uttar Pradesh, India.\n- Rani Jhansi Marine National Park commemorates Lakshmibai, the Rani of Jhansi.\n- Middle Button Island National Park, together with North Button Island and South Button Island, forms part of Rani Jhansi Marine National Park off the coast of South Andaman Island.",
